{"pagination":{"maxPageableSet":"10000","numFound":1,"query":"name=Sevigny&limit=10&title=Brave the Wild River","limit":10,"start":0},"items":{"mods":{"@version":"3.8","titleInfo":[{"title":"Brave the wild river ","subTitle":"the untold story of two women who mapped the botany of the Grand Canyon "},{"@type":"alternative","title":"Untold story of two women who mapped the botany of the Grand Canyon"}],"name":{"@usage":"primary","@type":"personal","namePart":["Sevigny, Melissa L.,",{"@type":"date","#text":"1986-"}],"role":[{"roleTerm":{"@type":"text","#text":"creator"}},{"roleTerm":{"@type":"text","#text":"author"}}],"nameIdentifier":"https://id.oclc.org/worldcat/entity/E39PCjt8WmXwwXhPv6BgxqrqjP"},"typeOfResource":"text","genre":[{"@authority":"marcgt","#text":"bibliography"},{"@authority":"marcgt","#text":"biography"},{"@authority":"rdacontent","#text":"text"},{"@authority":"rdacontent","#text":"still image"},{"@authority":"rdacontent","#text":"cartographic image"},{"@authority":"aat","#text":"travelog (performed works genre)"},{"@authority":"fast","#text":"Biographies"},{"@authority":"fast","#text":"History"},{"@authority":"fast","#text":"Travel writing"},{"@authority":"lcgft","#text":"Travel writing"},{"@authority":"lcgft","#text":"Biographies"},{"@authority":"rvmgf","#text":"Récits de voyages."},{"@authority":"rvmgf","#text":"Biographies."}],"originInfo":[{"place":{"placeTerm":[{"@type":"code","@authority":"marccountry","#text":"nyu"},{"@type":"text","@authority":"marccountry","#text":"New York (State)"}]},"dateIssued":{"@encoding":"marc","#text":"2023"},"copyrightDate":{"@encoding":"marc","#text":"2023"},"issuance":"monographic","edition":"First edition."},{"@eventType":"publication","place":{"placeTerm":{"@type":"text","#text":"New York, NY :"}},"agent":{"namePart":"W.W. Norton & Company,","role":{"roleTerm":"publisher"}},"dateIssued":[2023]}],"language":{"languageTerm":[{"@type":"code","@authority":"iso639-2b","#text":"eng"},{"@type":"text","@authority":"iso639-2b","#text":"English"}]},"physicalDescription":[{"form":[{"@authority":"marcform","#text":"print"},{"@type":"media","@authority":"rdamedia","#text":"unmediated"},{"@type":"carrier","@authority":"rdacarrier","#text":"volume"}],"extent":"290 pages : black and white illustrations, map, portraits ; 24 cm"},{"form":{"@type":"Illustrative content","#text":"illustration"}},{"form":{"@type":"Illustrative content","#text":"map"}},{"form":{"@type":"Illustrative content","#text":"portrait"}},{"form":{"@type":"Color content","#text":"monochrome"}}],"abstract":{"@type":"Summary","#text":"The tale of two pioneering botanists and their historic boat trip down the Colorado River and through the Grand Canyon. In the summer of 1938, botanists Elzada Clover and Lois Jotter set off to run the Colorado River, accompanied by an ambitious and entrepreneurial expedition leader, a zoologist, and two amateur boatmen. With its churning waters and treacherous boulders, the Colorado was famed as the most dangerous river in the world. Journalists and veteran river runners boldly proclaimed that the motley crew would never make it out alive. But for Clover and Jotter, the expedition held a tantalizing appeal: no one had yet surveyed the plant life of the Grand Canyon, and they were determined to be the first. Through the vibrant letters and diaries of the two women, science journalist Melissa L. Sevigny traces their daring forty-three-day journey down the river, during which they meticulously cataloged the thorny plants that thrived in the Grand Canyon's secret nooks and crannies. Along the way, they chased a runaway boat, ran the river's most fearsome rapids, and turned the harshest critic of female river runners into an ally. Clover and Jotter's plant list, including four new cactus species, would one day become vital for efforts to protect and restore the river ecosystem. Brave the Wild River is an adventure of two women who risked their lives to make an unprecedented botanical survey of a defining landscape in the American West, at a time when human influences had begun to change it forever. -- Provided by publisher."},"tableOfContents":{"@type":"Contents","#text":"Prologue: Stranded -- On the borders of precipices -- Have you seen that river? -- A mighty poor place for women -- There goes the Mexican Hat! -- A beautiful pea-green boat -- Delayed -- Hell, yes! What river? -- Paradise -- A most unusual and hazardous means -- A hundred personalities -- Lonely for the river -- Heaven as I go along -- Legendary -- Epilogue: A woman's place."},"note":[{"@type":"statement of responsibility","#text":"Melissa L. Sevigny."},{"@type":"bibliography","#text":"Includes bibliographical references (pages 263-280) and index."},"Council on Botanical and Horticultural Libraries (CBHL) Annual Literature Award - Nominee, 2024"],"subject":[{"geographicCode":[{"@authority":"marcgac","#text":"n-us-az"},{"@authority":"marcgac","#text":"n-us-ut"}]},{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":["Women travelers","History"],"geographic":["Arizona","Grand Canyon"],"temporal":"20th century"},{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":"Botanists","geographic":["Arizona","Grand Canyon"],"genre":"Biography"},{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":["Botany","History"],"geographic":["Arizona","Grand Canyon"],"temporal":"20th century"},{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":["Plant collecting","History"],"geographic":["Arizona","Grand Canyon"],"temporal":"20th century"},{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":["Scientific expeditions","History"],"geographic":["Arizona","Grand Canyon"],"temporal":"20th century"},{"@authority":"rvm","topic":["Voyageuses","Histoire"],"geographic":["Arizona","Grand Canyon"],"temporal":"20e siècle"},{"@authority":"rvm","topic":"Botanistes","geographic":["Arizona","Grand Canyon"],"genre":"Biographies"},{"@authority":"rvm","topic":["Plantes","Collectionneurs et collections","Histoire"],"geographic":["Arizona","Grand Canyon"],"temporal":"20e siècle"},{"@authority":"rvm","topic":["Expéditions scientifiques","Histoire